    // same address; [LOGO-START] is NOT removed). FUN_00259b20(a0=UIsub,
    // a1=request mask) is the mask->START iterator: for each set bit i in a1
    // that is NOT already armed (a1 & ~*a0 & (1<<i)) it dispatches FUN_00254ee0
    // on the channel at *(a0+0x208+i*4) (== mgr+0x7d8 slot i). §35 proved the 7
    // logo geom channels (slots 12,25-28,30,32; signature: channel ptr's +0x8c
    // is a real heap transform target in [0x100000,0x2000000)) are NEVER armed
    // on host (0/19 STARTs are geom), so they stay mode 0/size 0; retail arms
    // them to mode 1/size 1.0 (§34). This probe pins WHY the geom slots never
    // dispatch by deriving, per frame, a geom_mask from the live slot array and
    // intersecting it with the request mask and the already-armed set.
